          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Using a built-in font requires no additional files. According to the section “Standard Type 1 Fonts” in the PDF specification, “these fonts, or their font metrics and suitable substitution fonts, shall be available to the conforming reader.”"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can use an AFM font anywhere a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "font-family"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " key is recognized in the theme file. For example:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "base:\n  font-family: Times-Roman"
              }
            ],
            "language": "yaml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "However, when you use a built-in font, the characters you can use in your document are limited to the characters in the WINANSI ("
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Windows-1252"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "metadata": {
                  "rel": "noopener",
                  "window": "_blank"
                },
                "target": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows-1252"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") code set. WINANSI includes most of the characters needed for writing in Western languages (English, French, Spanish, etc). For anything outside of that, PDF is BYOF (Bring Your Own Font)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Even though the built-in fonts require the content to be encoded in WINANSI, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "you still type your AsciiDoc document in UTF-8"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". Asciidoctor PDF encodes the content into WINANSI when building the PDF."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Built-in (AFM) fonts do not use the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "fallback fonts"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "fallback-font.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". In order for the fallback font to kick in, you must use a TrueType font anywhere you want the fallback font to be used (e.g., the base font family, the code font family, etc)."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "warning"
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "When using the built-in PDF (AFM) fonts on a block of content in your AsciiDoc document, any character that cannot be encoded to WINANSI is replaced with a logic “not” glyph ("
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "¬"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ") and you’ll see the following warning in your console:"
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "literal",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "The following text could not be fully converted to the Windows-1252 character set:\n| <string with unknown glyph>"
                  }
                ],
                "language": null,
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "This behavior differs from the default behavior in Prawn, which is to simply crash."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "You’ll often see this warning if you’re using callouts in your document and you haven’t specified a TrueType font in your theme. To prevent this warning, you need to specify a TrueType font."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "When using a TrueType font, you will get no warning for a missing glyph. That’s a consequence of how Prawn works and is outside of Asciidoctor PDF’s control. However, you’ll likely see it substituted with a box (guaranteed if you’re using one of the bundled fonts)."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              },
              {
                "context": "paragraph",
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "For more information about how Prawn handles character encodings for built-in fonts, see "
                  },
                  {
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "this note in the Prawn CHANGELOG"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "link",
                    "metadata": {
                      "rel": "noopener",
                      "window": "_blank"
                    },
                    "target": "https://github.com/prawnpdf/prawn/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md#vastly-improved-handling-of-encodings-for-pdf-built-in-afm-fonts"
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "."
                  }
                ],
                "roles": [],
                "title": null
              }
            ],
            "context": "sidebar",
            "id": null,
            "roles": [],
            "title": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "WINANSI Encoding Behavior"
              }
            ]
          }
